## Losing weight

Losing **7 to 10% of your body weight** can reduce fat and inflammation in the liver, and may reverse early scarring. Lose weight gradually. Your GP may refer you to a weight management programme. Weight loss medicines or surgery may be offered to some people who qualify.

## Being active

Exercise helps even if your weight does not change. Aim for at least 150 minutes of moderate activity a week.

## Treating related conditions

Controlling **diabetes**, **blood pressure** and **cholesterol** protects your liver and your heart. Statins are safe for most people with fatty liver disease.

## Alcohol

Cut down, or stop drinking, especially if you have scarring. Your doctor will advise you.

## Specialist care

If you have advanced scarring, you will be seen by a liver specialist and have regular checks for liver cancer and other complications.
